---
import { Image } from "astro:assets";
import Layout from "@/layouts/Layout.astro";
import workshop from "@/assets/about/workshop.jpg";
import cyrWheel from "@/assets/about/cyr-wheel.png";
---

<Layout
  title="About"
  description="Hightopp Leather is the studio of Shawn Cook — leather artist, wildland firefighter, cyr wheel performer."
>
  <section class="container-prose pt-20 md:pt-28">
    <p class="font-serif text-sm uppercase tracking-[0.3em] text-tan-600">
      The studio
    </p>
    <h1 class="mt-6 font-serif text-4xl leading-tight md:text-6xl">
      Shawn Cook makes things by hand.
    </h1>

    <div class="mt-10 space-y-6 text-lg leading-relaxed text-bark-800">
      <p>
        Leather artist. Wildland firefighter. World-class cyr wheel performer.
        He picked up a needle and a swivel knife somewhere along the way and
        never put them down.
      </p>
      <p>
        The studio keeps its own time. Half-formed blocks on every surface, a
        teapot warm too long, something always getting stitched before a show
        that started an hour ago. Hats first, ceremony second, ordinary
        somewhere far behind.
      </p>
      <p>
        Shawn trained with monks in China as a young adult, then earned his way
        through one of the world's leading circus schools. From there his life
        forked. Half the year he's on a fireline somewhere out west, working
        seventy-two hours straight in the dirt and the smoke. The other half
        he's on stage, spinning inside a steel hoop the size of a man — moving
        in a way most people only ever see once.
      </p>
    </div>

    <figure class="my-14 grid grid-cols-1 gap-3 sm:grid-cols-5 sm:items-start sm:gap-4">
      <Image
        src={workshop}
        alt="Shawn at his workbench, mid-stitch"
        widths={[400, 600, 800]}
        sizes="(min-width: 640px) 40vw, 100vw"
        quality={90}
        class="h-auto w-full sm:col-span-2"
      />
      <Image
        src={cyrWheel}
        alt="Shawn performing on a cyr wheel under stage lights"
        widths={[600, 900, 1200]}
        sizes="(min-width: 640px) 60vw, 100vw"
        quality={90}
        class="h-auto w-full sm:col-span-3"
      />
    </figure>

    <div class="space-y-6 text-lg leading-relaxed text-bark-800">
      <p>
        Leather is what he comes home to. Top hats first — the kind of hats you
        wear once and remember forever. Then bags, goggles, masks, crowns.
        Anything a body can wear that needs to hold a story.
      </p>
      <p>
        Each piece is hand-cut from a single sheet of vegetable-tanned leather.
        Wet-formed over a sculpted block, saddle-stitched in waxed linen, dyed
        and painted in the studio.
      </p>
      <p class="font-serif text-2xl text-bark-900 italic">
        Built for stages, ceremonies, unbirthdays, and the kind of evenings
        you don't forget.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>
</Layout>
